ates - C) Obesity rates - D) Blood pressure - ****","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Respiratory Medicine","topicOriginal":"Respiratory Medicine","subtopic":"Copd","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Respiratory Medicine","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c8f7a117adf6","stem":"**Which factor did the study NOT consider in estimating COPD’s economic burden?** - A) Treatment costs - B) Labor supply impact - C) Work experience differences - D) Tourism revenue - ****","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Respiratory Medicine","topicOriginal":"Respiratory Medicine","subtopic":"Copd","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Respiratory Medicine","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f85989c54e92","stem":"**Which publication year is relevant for the constant prices used in the study’s economic estimates?** - A) 2015 - B) 2016 - C) 2017 - D) 2018 - ****","type":"Short Answer","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-64c5b28a94cf","stem":"**The study calls for urgent investment in what type of efforts?** - A) Developing new recreational drugs - B) Enhancing educational facilities - C) Effective interventions against COPD - D) Increasing tobacco production - **** These questions and answers provide a comprehensive overview of the key findings and implications of the study.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Respiratory Medicine","topicOriginal":"Respiratory Medicine","subtopic":"Copd","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Respiratory Medicine","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f99ad783f57d","stem":"Results based management includes","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Planning, implementing and monitoring"},{"label":"B","text":"Planning and monitoring and evaluation"},{"label":"C","text":"The monitoring and evaluation phase only"},{"label":"D","text":"The planning phase only"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-dca64feafa31","stem":"Monitoring and Evaluation are","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The same"},{"label":"B","text":"Different. Monitoring is the routine collection of information to track progress, evaluation is used to determine the relevance and fulfilment of objectives, developmental efficiency, effectiveness, impact and sustainability"},{"label":"C","text":"Different. Monitoring systems are determined during the planning phase while evaluation is determined at the end of the project or program"},{"label":"D","text":"The same. Only evaluation suffices in result based management"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-336617689481","stem":"The different steps of project or program cycle are","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Plan, implement, monitor, evaluate"},{"label":"B","text":"Initial assessment, planning, implementation, evaluate"},{"label":"C","text":"Initial assessment, planning, implement, monitor, evaluate"},{"label":"D","text":"Planning, implement, monitor, evaluate"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-4908e061335f","stem":"What does a monitoring and evaluation framework include?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Objectives, assumptions, indicators and a summary of activities"},{"label":"B","text":"Objectives and indicators"},{"label":"C","text":"Goal and objectives"},{"label":"D","text":"Goal, objectives and indicators"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-bdc18648ee26","stem":"What the difference between an M&E framework, a performance framework and a performance monitoring plan (PMP)?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The M&E framework measures program performance and the others measure staff performance"},{"label":"B","text":"Only the M&E framework has inputs and process, outputs, outcomes and impact"},{"label":"C","text":"They all serve the same purpose"},{"label":"D","text":"The PMP is the only one that details on indicators and means of measuring them"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","sub